  "question": {
    "text": "Power applied to a particle varies with time as <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> watt, where <math><mi>t</mi></math> is in second. What is the change in its kinetic energy (in joule)&nbsp;between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>?"
  },
